<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Holidays boost Australia air travel 9.6 pct.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Holidays boost Australia air travel 9.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>School holidays in most Australian states boosted domestic air travel in July, with a 9.6 percent jump in the number of revenue passengers carried over the previous month, the Transport Department said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Qantas Airways Ltd maintained its market lead over rival Ansett Australia, with almost 54 percent of total revenue passenger kilometres.</p>
</text>
